Build 034 (from the 033 run: crash at 383 s, pool largest free 2 MiB, app heap 2176 -> 2432 MiB at the end):
- The NUP container's cache of decompressed zstd members is capped by EDEN_NX2_NUP_CACHE_MIB
  (headless/main.cpp: 64 MiB on the console, nup-cache-mib.txt overrides; it was 512 MiB). It is app
  heap, whose pieces are never given back, in the 12 GiB pool the guest and graphics share. Members
  over half the cap are decompressed to a temporary file, as the largest ones already were.
- EDEN_NUP_CACHE log lines: the cap at start, then the cache's fill every 64 MiB.

